MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Minimum Qualifications: 1. Demonstrated ability to perform the duties described above using the theories, principles, practices, and techniques of generally accepted accounting principles. Work experience should include:
a. Interpreting and assessing program financial performance using standard financial management systems;
b. Interpreting balance sheet and profit and loss statement results:
c. Applying commercial budgeting techniques;
d. Supervisory experience directing technical and professional financial management operations. 2. Progressively responsible work experience in budget or finance that provided the incumbent the knowledge of appropriated fund and nonappropriated fund regulations on budgetary processes and requirements is required. The work experience must demonstrate the knowledge and ability to balance funds between accounts; i.e. transferring funds between line items or sub-projects or identifying excess funds for possible transfer to other operating programs. 3. Must have excellent organizational skills; be highly skilled in written and verbal communications and able to deal tactfully and effectively with employees in all levels of the organization. 4. Must be proficient in Microsoft Windows, Word, Excel, and other software as required, and be able to meet stringent deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Highly Preferred Criteria: 1. A minimum of five (5) years experience that demonstrates the ability to apply financial accounting principles, methods and techniques of fiscal management, and a strong background in budget preparation, payroll management, internal controls and financial systems reporting. 2. Experience coordinating manpower and staffing issues with NAF Personnel Office, E-Pay and Installation Management and Employee Tracking System. 3. Experience analyzing monthly financial reports to include budget variance, Capital Purchase and Minor Construction execution and cash flow projections. 4. Financial Management experience necessary to execute an effective acquisition and financial management plan to include demonstrated ability to determine resource needs and allocation of resources for both Appropriated Funds (APF) and Non-Appropriated Funds (NAF) budget and analysis for financial data. 5. Experience working with the following programs: Installation Management and Employee Tracking System, E-Pay, Financial Management Business System (FMBS), CEDMS-NAF (formally OLRV), Standard Management Information Reports for Finance (SMIRF), Recreation Tracking System (RECTRAC), Child Youth Management Tracking (CYMSTRAC) and Standard NAF Automated Contracting System (SNACs). **In order to be considered highly preferred, your resume must show that you meet BOTH the minimum qualifications, and ALL of the high preferred criteria. Applicants meeting ALL criteria will be referred to the selecting official first. Remaining applicants will be referred for consideration if the certificate (referral list) is returned with no selection.

